# Every path in this repository is owned by one person.
#
# This file is only half the mechanism: it names the owner, and the ruleset on
# main ("Require review from Code Owners") is what makes the name binding. A
# pull request from anyone else cannot merge without an approving review from
# the owner below, which is the point — outside contributions are welcome, but
# nothing lands unreviewed.
#
# The glob is deliberately broad rather than a list of per-directory rules.
# A narrower set of patterns would imply there are paths with a different
# owner, and there aren't; a path that matched nothing would silently need no
# code owner review at all.

